{"title":"Desert Dairy","sub":"Should a dairy company build a new plant?","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Food manufacturing","geo":"Saudi Arabia","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"30-35 min","skills":"Demand vs capacity · timing · cheaper alternatives first","prompt":"Desert Dairy is a leading dairy producer in Saudi Arabia. Its one plant can produce 500 million litres a year and is running at 460M litres. Demand is growing ~7% a year. The board is considering a new $150M plant that would add 200M litres of capacity. Should they build it?","clarify":[{"q":"Profit per litre?","a":"Contribution ≈ $0.30 per litre."},{"q":"Construction time?","a":"About 3 years from decision to production."},{"q":"Other options?","a":"Engineers say $20M of upgrades could squeeze 60M more litres from the existing plant within a year."},{"q":"Competitors?","a":"Two competitors have also announced expansions."}],"structure":{"root":"Build a new plant?","branches":[{"head":"Demand","items":["Our growth vs market growth","Is 7% sustainable?","Product mix"]},{"head":"Supply","items":["Our capacity & upgrades","Competitor capacity → price risk","Outsourcing to co-packers"]},{"head":"Economics","items":["Investment, contribution, payback","Timing vs 3-year build"]},{"head":"Risks","items":["Overcapacity","Execution","Raw milk supply"]}]},"hypothesis":"They will need more capacity, but the cheap upgrade should come first. The real question is when to commit to the new plant, given the 3-year build.","questions":[{"q":"When does Desert Dairy run out of capacity?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<table class=\"data mini\"><tr><td>Year</td><td class=\"r\">0</td><td class=\"r\">1</td><td class=\"r\">2</td><td class=\"r\">3</td><td class=\"r\">4</td><td class=\"r\">5</td></tr> <tr><td>Demand (M litres, +7%/yr)</td><td class=\"r\">460</td><td class=\"r\">492</td><td class=\"r\">527</td><td class=\"r\">564</td><td class=\"r\">603</td><td class=\"r\">645</td></tr></table> <p>Current plant (500M) runs out in <b>year 2</b>. With the $20M upgrade (560M) it's enough until <b>year 3</b>, when demand reaches 564M. A new plant takes 3 years, so <b>the decision has to be made now</b> to have capacity by year 3-4.</p>"},{"q":"Is the $20M upgrade worth it?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Extra volume sold: year 2 ≈ 27M litres (527 − 500) → $8M; year 3 onwards the full 60M litres → $18M/yr. Payback ≈ <b>2.5–3 years</b> from today ($0 in year 1, $8M in year 2, $18M in year 3), even if the new plant later takes over this volume. Easily worth it, and it buys time.</p>"},{"q":"Here is the industry picture. Does this change anything?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"305.8pt\" height=\"181.412pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 305.8 181.412\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\">\n <metadata>\n  <rdf:RDF xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:cc=\"http://creativecommons.org/ns#\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\">\n   <cc:Work>\n    <dc:type rdf:resource=\"http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/StillImage\"/>\n    <dc:date>2026-11-06T21:01:25.349449</dc:date>\n    <dc:format>image/svg+xml</dc:format>\n    <dc:creator>\n     <cc:Agent>\n      <dc:title>Matplotlib v3.11.2, https://matplotlib.org/</dc:title>\n     </cc:Agent>\n    </dc:creator>\n   </cc:Work>\n  </rdf:RDF>\n </metadata>\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 181.412 \nL 305.8 181.412 \nL 305.8 0 \nL 0 0 \nL 0 181.412 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 19.6 155.512 \nL 298.6 155.512 \nL 298.6 28 \nL 19.6 28 \nL 19.6 155.512 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\">\n    <g id=\"xtick_1\">\n     <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n      <defs>\n       <path id=\"mda1b199307\" d=\"M 0 0 \nL 0 3.5 \n\" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; 